<description>&lt;p&gt;Mexico's president Claudia Sheinbaum is accusing the U.S. DEA of interference after the agency launched an anonymous cartel tip line, prompting Mexico to file a complaint with the United States and reject the initiative. The controversy intensified as Mexico opened investigations into former prosecutor Guillermo Zuany for alleged CIA and cartel ties, while a separate bus crash in Mexico killed five Arizona sisters and injured dozens. Meanwhile, a high-profile cartel leader, El Chapo Isidro, was captured by Mexican special forces with U.S. drone support, sparking concerns about a violent succession battle within the cartel. 37 battle-related deaths were recorded in 1996, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxPVndYQjRrcDJpX3ZNTl82RXdmSzJsWmUwMl9wdzB5MVlaTkUtTjlMQjFINjd6ZkZpNUhWelhGNk5TenV4dGVZd05SNTlpbXBQajRsb09nQ3JmZ0E2WnIxYklTS3VmclA0dVRDSGhCU2VuWGhKeHRCdW00akRyMVZLQ3V5MzFUd3ljV1M3VURnUFhmRTdzNTBBV1lwdmhMcU9WODFIc0xHR29hZ25zOXJWOXp0Mkc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxQazNnUkZVd0Q0NHp4Szc1Xy16YmhLMXJJbm1NRy11R29xV0RvNEtoRkpFV2RtR0tvZ2xOeXBCYk8xTUR3amFzX0MwSjVtVFM2TUtHV2FpNWg2UDIzckZvNUdoampycG0yZFJubEd5b1NEcW5LNk9iQ1ZURVhZVnJMTkZDS2RGMDNOR1BRcWJGSDVxYjN6cTdJcG5ERV9qdTlGUDBXbDhFSHk3YlU?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Economist&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwgFBVV95cUxOUm9KTnF2aG4xTXRUYWZGeDgycjZwSElpWXYxQ09uX1FuQVMxMUcyUXdEdWxKbVR5M09Ja2pSa3A0dzM4VkFOVFdlQWJXbVlTWk1oVFV2cmc5YWFzU3BxdUV5SE0xck4ydndUZ0lyVzhWNmJqaVN1RTc1Qk11X2hNVzgtNUZib0FtV3ktN2ZzdGc3blR1T1VZRlpUYVNSY1oyMXgzREtIQ0FfdGo2WDVNcGdrVEVleUltNG5sRWtWdi03dw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxPdTJWOWx0TWc0em5CMlg1QlM3TXM4UndMM3JoekpiMnpBe